This report was prepared and submitted by Codex, an AI coding agent, on behalf of the repository operator.

## What issue are you seeing?

Current `main` accepts an arbitrarily large MultiAgentV2 `usage_hint_text` and appends it unchanged to the model-visible `spawn_agent` tool description.

Reproduced at commit `44b857c00e5803adedbc5b2e94c4a33574a157fe` on September 22, 2026. A 40,000-byte hint produced a final rendered description of 41,075 bytes and 10,269 estimated tokens. The complete hint, fixed generic tool guidance, and fixed markers were all present.

The relevant current path is:

- `codex-rs/core/src/tools/handlers/multi_agents_spec.rs`: `create_spawn_agent_tool_v2` appends `usage_hint_text` directly.
- `codex-rs/core/src/session/multi_agents.rs`: configured/composed role text is preserved without a final-size admission check.
- `codex-rs/prompts/src/multi_agent_instructions.rs`: configured or composed instructions are rendered without a final-size admission check.

This conflicts with the repository's model-visible context rule in root `AGENTS.md`: no individual item may exceed 10K tokens.

The same class can affect configured, composed, inherited, or restored usage hints because the final rendered content is not checked at the model-visible boundary. This report demonstrates the generic V2 tool-description path directly.

## What steps can reproduce the bug?

1. Check out `44b857c00e5803adedbc5b2e94c4a33574a157fe`.
2. Add this focused test beside the existing `multi_agents_spec` tests:

```rust
use codex_utils_output_truncation::approx_token_count;

#[test]
fn spawn_agent_tool_v2_accepts_generic_usage_hint_above_ten_thousand_tokens() {
    const HINT_PREFIX: &str = "USAGE_HINT_LIMIT_PREFIX";
    const HINT_SUFFIX: &str = "USAGE_HINT_LIMIT_SUFFIX";

    let usage_hint_text = format!("{HINT_PREFIX}\n{}\n{HINT_SUFFIX}", "x".repeat(40_000));
    let ToolSpec::Function(ResponsesApiTool { description, .. }) = create_spawn_agent_tool_v2(
        SpawnAgentToolOptions {
            multi_agent_version: MultiAgentVersion::V2,
            usage_hint_text: Some(usage_hint_text.clone()),
            ..Default::default()
        },
        /*description_override*/ None,
    ) else {
        panic!("spawn_agent should be a function tool");
    };

    assert!(approx_token_count(&description) > 10_000);
    assert!(description.contains("Spawns an agent to work on the specified task."));
    assert!(description.contains(&usage_hint_text));
    assert!(description.ends_with(HINT_SUFFIX));
}
```

3. Run the focused `codex-core` test.
4. Observe that it passes. In this reproduction, the final description measured 10,269 estimated tokens.

The reproduction ran on Linux WSL2 x86-64 with Rust 1.94.0. It did not submit the oversized schema to a provider; the defect occurs before provider request construction.

## What is the expected behavior?

Codex should enforce the existing 10K model-visible item contract against the complete final rendered usage-hint content, including fixed markers and tool-description overhead, before the description reaches model-visible context.

Oversized effective content should fail explicitly rather than being silently accepted. The check should cover every route that can produce the same final usage hint, including configured, composed, inherited, restored, and generic tool-description content.

## Additional information

Tracker searches performed immediately before filing found related but distinct reports:

- #40526 covers unbounded successful subagent completion messages, not spawn-tool usage hints.
- #41703 covers unintended whitespace in the same description builder, not size admission.
- #36973 covers conflicting delegation guidance, not an oversized single model-visible item.

No existing issue found in the searched open and closed tracker results reports this source-to-sink path or the demonstrated over-10K final description.
